  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Credential Stuffing: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Credential Stuffing: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What It Is",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Credential stuffing== replays username/password pairs **leaked from other sites**",
                "The bet: ==password reuse==",
                "Not guessing: only **1-2 tries** per account"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Three Attacks Compared",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Attack",
                "Passwords",
                "Accounts"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Brute force",
                  "many",
                  "one"
                ],
                [
                  "Password spraying",
                  "a few common",
                  "many"
                ],
                [
                  "Stuffing",
                  "known real pair",
                  "many, one pair each"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Why Lockout Misses It",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Spread over **thousands of accounts**",
                "Rotating ==residential-proxy IPs==",
                "No single IP or account trips a threshold"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "High login ==failure ratio==",
                "Many distinct usernames per IP or **device fingerprint**",
                "Spike in ==401s==",
                "Success rate only about ==0.1-2%=="
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Layered Defense",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Throttle",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Challenge",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Second factor",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Block known-bad passwords",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "No silver bullet",
              "text": "Stuffing uses **real** passwords from many IPs, so ==no single control is enough==. Stack the layers."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Rate Limiting by IP and Account",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Rate Limiting by IP and Account",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Two Keys, Both Needed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Key",
                "Stops",
                "Bypassed by"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**Per-IP**",
                  "one noisy source",
                  "rotating proxy IPs"
                ],
                [
                  "**Per-account**",
                  "many IPs on one user",
                  "spreading over many accounts"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Algorithms and Counters",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:Fixed window}: simple, but a ==2x burst== fits at the window edge",
                "==Sliding window== or **token bucket** smooths the burst",
                "Store counters in ==Redis==: `INCR`, then `EXPIRE` on first hit"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "INCR fail:acct:alice",
                "EXPIRE fail:acct:alice 900",
                "INCR fail:ip:203.0.113.7",
                "EXPIRE fail:ip:203.0.113.7 900"
              ],
              "note": "900 s = 15 min window"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:5 failed attempts} per account per 15 min",
                "{green:20 failed attempts} per IP per 15 min",
                "Count ==failures==, not total requests"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Proxy and Response Rules",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Behind a proxy or CDN, read the IP from a ==trusted X-Forwarded-For hop== only",
                "Raw header trusted: attacker spoofs a **new IP every request**",
                "Over limit: return ==429== with a `Retry-After` header",
                "Unknown and known usernames: **same response and timing**, no enumeration"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Two keys, failures only, trusted hop only, 429 plus `Retry-After`, identical answers."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Progressive Delays and Account Lockout",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Progressive Delays and Account Lockout",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Progressive Delay",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "1s",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "2s",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "4s",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "8s",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "... 15 min cap",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Exponential backoff: the wait ==doubles== after each failure",
                "Guessing gets slow; the user is **not** locked out"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Hard Lockout",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Account disabled after ==N failures==, until timeout or manual reset",
                "{green:Strong} against single-account guessing",
                "{red:DoS risk}: attacker sends bad passwords to lock victims out"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Safer Pattern and Trade-offs",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Soft lock per ==(username, IP or device)== pair",
                "Or a temporary lock that auto-expires, with CAPTCHA or email unlock"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Control",
                "Strength",
                "Weakness"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Lockout",
                  "Protects the account",
                  "Attacker can lock user out"
                ],
                [
                  "Delay",
                  "Stays available",
                  "Slower to deter"
                ],
                [
                  "Per-IP limit",
                  "Stops one source",
                  "Easy to rotate around"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Delay vs lockout?** Delay keeps access; lockout stops guessing but allows DoS.",
                "**How does lockout hurt users?** Attackers lock victims with bad passwords.",
                "**Safer design?** Temporary soft lock per username+device, with CAPTCHA or email unlock."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Never permanent",
              "text": "Lock ==temporarily==, key it on a **pair**, and give users a way back in."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "CAPTCHA and Multi-Factor Authentication",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "CAPTCHA and Multi-Factor Authentication",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. CAPTCHA as Friction",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Show it only after ==N failures== or a high risk score",
                "Not on every login: normal users are not penalised",
                "Solving farms and AI solvers win for ==a few cents== per solve",
                "Friction, **not** a security boundary"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Client",
                    "sub": "gets token",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Server",
                    "sub": "POST siteverify",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Provider",
                    "sub": "success?",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Login check",
                    "sub": "only if valid",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Verify ==server-side==: a client-only check is trivially bypassed",
                "Tokens are **single-use** and expire"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "curl -d \"secret=$SECRET\" -d \"response=$TOKEN\" \\",
                "  https://www.google.com/recaptcha/api/siteverify"
              ],
              "note": "provider's siteverify endpoint"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. MFA Ranking and Gotchas",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Rank",
                "Factor",
                "Weakness"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "1",
                  "==Passkeys / WebAuthn==",
                  "phishing-resistant"
                ],
                [
                  "2",
                  "TOTP app",
                  "code can be phished"
                ],
                [
                  "3",
                  "Push",
                  "MFA fatigue"
                ],
                [
                  "4",
                  "SMS",
                  "SIM-swap"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Rate-limit the ==OTP step== too: 6 digits = only 1M values",
                "Approval spam wears users down on push",
                "SIM-swap hijacks SMS codes"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "MFA makes a ==stuffed password alone useless==. CAPTCHA only slows bots."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
